@@ -97,3 +97,7 @@ The following bug fixes are included in the 3.4 release:
 
 * Extension entry-points are only loaded if needed (#1216).
 * Added additional checks to the `<pre><code>` handling of `PrettifyTreeprocessor` (#1261, #1263).
+* Backslash-escaped characters are now restored by a new `UnescapeTreeprocessor`
+  before serialization, so they are properly escaped in the output. Previously,
+  an escaped quote (for example, `![x\"x](x)` with the `smarty` extension) could
+  produce invalid HTML in attribute values.
